B.a4Z=s(["We keep this simple: here is what we collect, why, and who we share it with. This applies to the Sokie beta in the United States."],t.s)
B.a1q=new A.d3("Our promise",B.a4Z)
B.a42=s(["\u2022 Account & profile: your name, email, phone, password, and addresses.","\u2022 Jobs: task details, locations, scheduling, messages, photos, and reviews you provide.","\u2022 Location: your device location to match and route jobs, and a Runner\u2019s live location while a job is active.","\u2022 Payments: handled by Stripe. We receive limited details (like card type and last four digits) and do not store full card numbers.","\u2022 Runner verification: for Runners, identity verification through Stripe Identity (which may include an ID and selfie, handled by Stripe), and any license, insurance, or background information where used.","\u2022 Device & usage: basic app and device information to keep Sokie working and safe."],t.s)
B.a1d=new A.d3("1. Information we collect",B.a42)
B.a2M=s(["To run the service and match jobs; process payments and payouts; verify identity and keep the community safe; provide support and send service updates and reminders; and improve Sokie. We send marketing only where allowed and you can opt out anytime."],t.s)
B.a1p=new A.d3("2. How we use it",B.a2M)
B.a44=s(["\u2022 The other person on a job (customer and Runner), so the job can be done \u2014 for example name, task, location, and live tracking.","\u2022 Service providers that help us operate: Stripe (payments & identity), maps/geocoding, notifications, and secure cloud hosting. They may only use the data to provide their service to us.","\u2022 Legal & safety reasons, when required by law or to protect people.","We do not sell your personal information."],t.s)
B.a10=new A.d3("3. Who we share it with",B.a44)
B.a56=s(["Sokie currently operates in the United States, and your data is processed in the U.S. by us and our service providers."],t.s)
B.a1n=new A.d3("4. Where your data is handled",B.a56)
B.a5q=s(["You can access, update, or delete your information, and manage notifications in the app or by contacting us. Depending on your U.S. state (for example, California), you may have additional privacy rights \u2014 just reach out and we will help. Email privacy@sokie.com."],t.s)
B.a0X=new A.d3("5. Your choices & rights",B.a5q)
B.a50=s(["We use reasonable measures to protect your data, including encryption in transit and access controls. No system is perfectly secure. We keep information only as long as needed to run the service and meet legal and business requirements."],t.s)
B.a0W=new A.d3("6. Security & retention",B.a50)
B.a3X=s(["Sokie is for adults (18+). We do not knowingly collect information from children."],t.s)
B.a0V=new A.d3("7. Children",B.a3X)
B.a5a=s(["We may update this policy and will post the new version in the app. Questions or requests: privacy@sokie.com. (Sokie)"],t.s)
B.a1r=new A.d3("8. Changes & contact",B.a5a)
B.a31=s([B.a1q,B.a1d,B.a1p,B.a10,B.a1n,B.a0X,B.a0W,B.a0V,B.a1r],t.J8)
B.xa=new A.Am("privacy","Privacy Policy",u.A,B.a31)
B.a3M=s(["Sokie is in an early testing release, available in the United States only. Features may change and occasional issues are expected. These plain-language terms apply during the beta and will be replaced by full terms at public launch. By creating an account or using Sokie, you agree to them."],t.s)
B.a1h=new A.d3("About this beta",B.a3M)
B.a3_=s(["You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter into a contract. Please provide accurate information and keep your account secure. You are responsible for activity on your account."],t.s)
B.a15=new A.d3("1. Who can use Sokie",B.a3_)
B.a2X=s(['Sokie is a marketplace that connects customers with independent workers and businesses ("Runners") for everyday errands and home and skilled services.',"Sokie is a platform that makes introductions and handles booking and payment. It does not perform the services and does not employ Runners. The agreement to do the actual work is between you and the Runner."],t.s)
B.a13=new A.d3("2. What Sokie is",B.a2X)
B.a3Z=s(["You post a job, set a price or receive a quote or bids, a Runner is matched, the work is done, and you confirm it is complete in the app. For some jobs a Runner may suggest an add-on, which you can approve or decline."],t.s)
B.a1j=new A.d3("3. How it works",B.a3Z)
B.a2T=s(["Payments are handled securely by Stripe. When you book, your card is authorized (held) for the amount shown.","You are charged only after the job is completed and confirmed, and only up to the amount held. If the final amount is lower, we capture less and release the rest. The price is the Runner\u2019s quote plus Sokie\u2019s service fee, which uses declining rates on each Runner\u2019s quote: 20% of the first $20, 15% of the next $30, 10% of the next $50 and 5% of anything above $100 (for example, a $200 quote has an $18.50 fee). Tips are optional and go entirely to the Runner. Fees are shown before you confirm. Jobs booked before October 11, 2026 keep the fees shown when they were booked.","Confirming completed work: when a Runner marks a job complete, you have 24 hours to confirm it. If you do not confirm within that time and there is no open dispute, the job is automatically confirmed and your card is charged for the work done (up to the amount held). This makes sure Runners are paid for work they have completed. If something is wrong, contact support or open a dispute before the 24 hours pass.","If something goes wrong, contact support and we will help resolve it. Refunds may be issued at our discretion and as required by law."],t.s)
B.a0U=new A.d3("4. Payments",B.a2T)
B.a2V=s(["Give accurate job details and safe access to the location. Services may happen in or around your home and carry everyday risks, so please secure valuables, pets, and hazards. Treat Runners with respect. You are responsible for using Sokie lawfully."],t.s)
B.a1b=new A.d3("5. Your responsibilities & safety",B.a2V)
B.a4D=s(["Some jobs (like plumbing, electrical, or HVAC) may legally require a licensed professional. Any badges or verification we show are to help you, not a guarantee. You are responsible for making sure a Runner is right and qualified for your job."],t.s)
B.a1_=new A.d3("6. Licensed & skilled work",B.a4D)
B.a4G=s(["You can post reviews, photos, and messages. Only post content you have the right to share, and nothing unlawful or abusive. You let Sokie use that content to run and improve the service. We may remove content that breaks these terms."],t.s)
B.a12=new A.d3("7. Reviews & content",B.a4G)
B.a3o=s(["Do not use Sokie for anything illegal, harassing, deceptive, or unsafe; do not try to arrange jobs off-platform to avoid fees; and do not disrupt, copy, or misuse the app."],t.s)
B.a16=new A.d3("8. Things you agree not to do",B.a3o)
B.a4z=s(["\u2022 Illegal, stolen, counterfeit or hazardous items \u2014 including illegal drugs (marijuana is illegal in Tennessee), firearms, ammunition, explosives, fireworks and hazardous chemicals. Runners may refuse any item they reasonably believe falls into these groups.","\u2022 Animals other than dogs and cats. Pet transport is limited to dogs and cats, and you must tell us about anything that affects safe handling (size, temperament, crate).","\u2022 Picking up, transporting, watching or waiting with children or minors. Child pickup and child care are not offered.","\u2022 Passenger rides outside the Private Ride and Carpool services. Private Rides are matched only with drivers whose ID, background check, driver's license, insurance and vehicle have been verified. Riders must be adults (18+); children and minors may not ride. Riders must wear seatbelts and follow the driver's reasonable safety instructions, and the driver may decline or end a ride that feels unsafe.","Posting a job that breaks these rules may lead to cancellation without refund of fees and suspension of your account."],t.s)
B.a18=new A.d3("8a. What Sokie won't carry or do",B.a4z)
B.a3l=s(["Carpool lets drivers share empty seats with riders going the same way, on a regular route or a one-time trip on chosen dates. Sokie suggests a fair seat price based on the driver\u2019s running costs; drivers set their own price up to a cap, and riders may offer a different price, which the driver can accept, counter or decline. Sokie charges riders a booking fee of 10% of the seat price (minimum $0.75); drivers pay no fee.","Riders must be adults (18+). Riders meet the driver at the listed meeting point; drivers do not pick up at home addresses. Seats can be booked up to 60 days ahead. Your card is held before each trip (trips more than 6 days away are reserved on your saved card and held 6 days before) and charged after the trip. If a held or reserved seat can\u2019t be held on your card, it is released.","Rider cancellations: free until 24 hours before departure. Between 24 and 2 hours before departure, 50% of the seat price (plus the booking fee) is charged; within 2 hours of departure, or if you don\u2019t show up, the full seat price is charged. That amount goes to the driver for the seat they kept for you.","Driver cancellations: if a driver cancels a trip, stops a route or removes a rider, riders are released and never charged. A driver cancellation or removal within 24 hours of departure counts as a late cancellation (removals for safety reasons do not); three late cancellations within 60 days pauses the driver\u2019s routes for review. Drivers may remove a rider and choose not to carry them again.","Waitlist: when a trip is full you can join its waitlist. If a seat opens, the first rider on the waitlist is booked automatically on their saved card and notified; the normal cancellation terms then apply. You can leave the waitlist at any time.","Carpool drivers must pass the same checks as Private Ride drivers (ID, background check, clean record, driver\u2019s license, insurance and vehicle) and are responsible for insurance that covers their passengers."],t.s)
B.a17=new A.d3("8b. Carpool",B.a3l)
B.a3Y=s(['Sokie is provided "as is" during beta. We do not guarantee it will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that any Runner or service will meet your expectations. Nothing here removes rights you have under the law that cannot be waived.'],t.s)
