B.a2l=s(["Thanks for helping test Sokie. Here is how working through Sokie works during the beta. These are in addition to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy."],t.s)
B.a19=new A.d3("For Runners",B.a2l)
B.a5v=s(["You run your own independent business. You are not an employee of Sokie. You choose which jobs to accept, when to work, and how to do the work, and you can work elsewhere. You are responsible for your own taxes, equipment, and expenses."],t.s)
B.a1f=new A.d3("1. You are an independent contractor",B.a5v)
B.a4J=s(["You must personally perform the jobs you accept. Subcontracting, delegating, or sending someone else in your place is not allowed, and you may not share, sell, or transfer your Sokie account. The person we verify is the person who does the work (for a business account, the verified business and its own vetted workers). Violations can result in removal from the platform."],t.s)
B.a1e=new A.d3("1a. No subcontracting",B.a4J)
B.a3N=s(["You must be 18+, legally allowed to do the work, and complete onboarding, which may include identity verification (via Stripe Identity) and, where it applies, background or credential checks. Keep your information accurate."],t.s)
B.a0Y=new A.d3("2. Getting started",B.a3N)
B.a2y=s(["You are responsible for holding any licenses, permits, and insurance the law requires for the work you offer \u2014 especially for skilled trades. Do not accept jobs you are not qualified or permitted to do. Please provide proof when asked.","Both individuals and businesses may offer licensed trades (e.g. plumbing, electrical, HVAC), but you must upload your license or trade certificate and be verified first. Until then, you will not see or be matched to licensed-trade jobs. The verified individual or business must personally perform the work \u2014 no subcontracting."],t.s)
B.a0Z=new A.d3("3. Licenses, insurance & verification",B.a2y)
B.a52=s(["For each completed job you receive your accepted quote minus Sokie\u2019s commission: 15% for most jobs, or 20% in a few categories, shown on the job. The commission applies only to job pay \u2014 never to tips (which are 100% yours) or to purchases you\u2019re reimbursed for \u2014 and you always see your exact payout before you accept. Customers pay their own separate service fee. If a customer cancels after you\u2019ve set out and a cancellation fee applies, 75% of it is paid to you. Jobs posted before October 11, 2026 keep their original terms. Payouts are made through Stripe Connect \u2014 you will set up a Stripe account and agree to Stripe\u2019s Connected Account terms. The customer\u2019s payment is held and released on completion; payout timing follows Stripe\u2019s schedule. Tips go to you.","After you mark a job complete, the customer has 24 hours to confirm it. If they do not confirm within that time and there is no open dispute, the job is automatically confirmed so you are paid for the work you completed."],t.s)
B.a1o=new A.d3("4. How you get paid",B.a52)
B.a5f=s(["You are responsible for reporting and paying your own taxes on what you earn. Sokie and/or Stripe may provide tax forms where required and may need to report certain information."],t.s)
B.a11=new A.d3("5. Taxes",B.a5f)
B.a2S=s(["Do the job professionally, safely, and lawfully; bring your own tools and transport unless agreed otherwise; communicate through the app; and get the customer\u2019s approval before doing extra work or changing the price.","Never carry illegal, stolen or hazardous items (illegal drugs, firearms, ammunition, explosives, fireworks, hazardous chemicals). Only transport dogs and cats. Do not pick up, transport, watch or wait with children or minors. Carry adult passengers only on a Private Ride job or a Carpool route or trip you posted (where you may charge no more than the seat-price cap), and only once Sokie has verified your driver's license, insurance and vehicle (in addition to your ID and background check); you are responsible for holding insurance that covers carrying paying passengers. If a job turns out to involve anything prohibited, stop and report it in the app \u2014 you will not be penalized for refusing."],t.s)
B.a1i=new A.d3("6. Doing the work",B.a2S)
B.a3j=s(["For jobs you get through Sokie, do not arrange payment off-platform to avoid fees or divert Sokie customers away from the app."],t.s)
B.a1c=new A.d3("7. Keep it on Sokie",B.a3j)
B.a58=s(["Use customer information only to do the job, keep it private, and do not reuse it for your own purposes."],t.s)
B.a1m=new A.d3("8. Customer information",B.a58)
B.a2K=s(["Your profile may show ratings and verification status. We may suspend or deactivate accounts for safety concerns, policy or legal violations, or loss of required credentials."],t.s)
B.a0S=new A.d3("9. Ratings & account",B.a2K)
B.a3k=s(['Sokie is provided "as is" during beta. To the extent the law allows, Sokie is not liable for indirect losses, and our responsibility to you is limited to the commissions we earned from your recent jobs. You can stop anytime, and we may end the beta or your access as described here.'],t.s)
B.a1a=new A.d3("10. Beta disclaimer, liability & ending",B.a3k)
B.a30=s(["Questions about Runner payments or your account: support@sokie.com. (Sokie)"],t.s)
